    'In use' => 'In use',
    '{n, plural, =1{Save the Standard draft as alt text on # image?} other{Save the Standard draft as alt text on # images?}} Drafts flagged Check are skipped.' => '{n, plural, =1{Save the Standard draft as alt text on # image?} other{Save the Standard draft as alt text on # images?}} Drafts flagged Check are skipped.',
    '{n, plural, =1{Approved # draft.} other{Approved # drafts.}}' => '{n, plural, =1{Approved # draft.} other{Approved # drafts.}}',
    '{n, plural, =1{# draft needs a check before it can be saved.} other{# drafts need a check before they can be saved.}}' => '{n, plural, =1{# draft needs a check before it can be saved.} other{# drafts need a check before they can be saved.}}',
    'Image has no alt text' => 'Image has no alt text',
    'Add an alt attribute to the image. If the image carries meaning, describe what it shows in a few words; if it is purely decorative, leave the alt empty (alt="") so screen readers skip it. For Craft assets, fill in the alt text on the asset and check the template outputs it.' => 'Add an alt attribute to the image. If the image carries meaning, describe what it shows in a few words; if it is purely decorative, leave the alt empty (alt="") so screen readers skip it. For Craft assets, fill in the alt text on the asset and check the template outputs it.',
    'Alt text is a filename' => 'Alt text is a filename',
    'Replace the filename with a few words describing what the image shows. This usually comes from a template printing the asset title instead of its alt text: output the alt field and fill it in on the asset.' => 'Replace the filename with a few words describing what the image shows. This usually comes from a template printing the asset title instead of its alt text: output the alt field and fill it in on the asset.',
    'Heading level skipped' => 'Heading level skipped',
    'Use heading levels in order without jumping a step, so an h2 is followed by another h2 or an h3, not an h4. Choose the level for where the heading sits in the page outline, and change how big it looks with CSS.' => 'Use heading levels in order without jumping a step, so an h2 is followed by another h2 or an h3, not an h4. Choose the level for where the heading sits in the page outline, and change how big it looks with CSS.',
    'Heading is empty' => 'Heading is empty',
    'Put text in the heading, or remove the heading if it is only there for spacing or decoration. The check reads the text inside the heading, so a heading holding only an image or an icon needs visually hidden text as well.' => 'Put text in the heading, or remove the heading if it is only there for spacing or decoration. The check reads the text inside the heading, so a heading holding only an image or an icon needs visually hidden text as well.',
    'More than one h1 on the page' => 'More than one h1 on the page',
    'Keep one h1 for the main heading of the page and use h2 and below for the sections under it. A logo or site name marked up as an h1 in the header is the usual second one.' => 'Keep one h1 for the main heading of the page and use h2 and below for the sections under it. A logo or site name marked up as an h1 in the header is the usual second one.',
    'Link has no name' => 'Link has no name',
    'Give the link text that says where it goes. For a link holding only an icon or an image, add alt text to the image or an aria-label to the link.' => 'Give the link text that says where it goes. For a link holding only an icon or an image, add alt text to the image or an aria-label to the link.',
    'Link text is too vague' => 'Link text is too vague',
    'Change the link text so it makes sense on its own, such as "Read the annual report" in place of "Read more". If the design needs the visible text kept short, add the rest as visually hidden text inside the link.' => 'Change the link text so it makes sense on its own, such as "Read the annual report" in place of "Read more". If the design needs the visible text kept short, add the rest as visually hidden text inside the link.',
    'Link opens a new tab without saying so' => 'Link opens a new tab without saying so',
    'Tell people before the link opens a new tab: add "opens in a new tab" to the link text (visually hidden if need be) or to its aria-label. Or remove target="_blank" so the link opens in the same tab.' => 'Tell people before the link opens a new tab: add "opens in a new tab" to the link text (visually hidden if need be) or to its aria-label. Or remove target="_blank" so the link opens in the same tab.',
    'Symbol used without words' => 'Symbol used without words',
    'Add visually hidden text saying what the symbol means, such as "Included" for a tick, and mark the symbol itself aria-hidden="true". For a link, give it real text saying where it goes.' => 'Add visually hidden text saying what the symbol means, such as "Included" for a tick, and mark the symbol itself aria-hidden="true". For a link, give it real text saying where it goes.',
    'Button has no name' => 'Button has no name',
    'Give the button text that says what it does. For an icon-only button, add an aria-label or visually hidden text inside it, or alt text on the image it holds.' => 'Give the button text that says what it does. For an icon-only button, add an aria-label or visually hidden text inside it, or alt text on the image it holds.',
    'Form field has no label' => 'Form field has no label',
    'Give each field a <label>, linked with a for attribute that matches the field\'s id, or wrap the field inside the label. Placeholder text does not count: it disappears as soon as someone starts typing.' => 'Give each field a <label>, linked with a for attribute that matches the field\'s id, or wrap the field inside the label. Placeholder text does not count: it disappears as soon as someone starts typing.',
    'Dropdown has no label' => 'Dropdown has no label',
    'Give the dropdown a <label> linked with a for attribute that matches the select\'s id. Where a visible label really cannot fit, use aria-label or aria-labelledby.' => 'Give the dropdown a <label> linked with a for attribute that matches the select\'s id. Where a visible label really cannot fit, use aria-label or aria-labelledby.',
    'Table has no header cells' => 'Table has no header cells',
    'Mark the header row or column with <th> cells in place of <td>, and add scope="col" or scope="row" to say which way each applies. If the table is only there for layout, add role="presentation" to it, or better, lay the content out with CSS.' => 'Mark the header row or column with <th> cells in place of <td>, and add scope="col" or scope="row" to say which way each applies. If the table is only there for layout, add role="presentation" to it, or better, lay the content out with CSS.',
    'Page language is not set' => 'Page language is not set',
    'Add a lang attribute to the <html> element in your layout template, such as lang="en", so screen readers pronounce the page in the right language. In Craft, craft.app.language gives the current site\'s language.' => 'Add a lang attribute to the <html> element in your layout template, such as lang="en", so screen readers pronounce the page in the right language. In Craft, craft.app.language gives the current site\'s language.',
    'Page has no title' => 'Page has no title',
    'Add a <title> element inside the page\'s <head> naming the page, then the site. In a Craft layout this usually comes from the entry title, or from an SEO plugin where you use one.' => 'Add a <title> element inside the page\'s <head> naming the page, then the site. In a Craft layout this usually comes from the entry title, or from an SEO plugin where you use one.',
    'No skip link' => 'No skip link',
    'Add a "Skip to main content" link as the first thing on the page, pointing at the id of your main content area. It can stay visually hidden until it takes keyboard focus.' => 'Add a "Skip to main content" link as the first thing on the page, pointing at the id of your main content area. It can stay visually hidden until it takes keyboard focus.',
    'No main landmark' => 'No main landmark',
    'Wrap the main content of the page in one <main> element in your layout template, so screen reader users can jump straight to it.' => 'Wrap the main content of the page in one <main> element in your layout template, so screen reader users can jump straight to it.',
    'No landmark regions' => 'No landmark regions',
    'Mark up the regions of the page with <header>, <nav>, <main> and <footer> in place of plain <div> elements. Screen reader users move between these regions to find their way around.' => 'Mark up the regions of the page with <header>, <nav>, <main> and <footer> in place of plain <div> elements. Screen reader users move between these regions to find their way around.',
    'Iframe has no title' => 'Iframe has no title',
    'Add a title attribute to the iframe saying what it holds, such as title="Map of our office" or title="Video: product tour". Embed codes from video and map services often leave it out.' => 'Add a title attribute to the iframe saying what it holds, such as title="Map of our office" or title="Video: product tour". Embed codes from video and map services often leave it out.',
    'Video has no captions' => 'Video has no captions',
    'Add a captions file to the video with a <track kind="captions"> element pointing at a WebVTT file. Captions burnt into the picture itself are not detected, so check those by eye.' => 'Add a captions file to the video with a <track kind="captions"> element pointing at a WebVTT file. Captions burnt into the picture itself are not detected, so check those by eye.',
    'Media plays sound on its own' => 'Media plays sound on its own',
    'Remove the autoplay attribute, or add muted so the media starts silently. If it has to play with sound, give people a visible control to pause or stop it.' => 'Remove the autoplay attribute, or add muted so the media starts silently. If it has to play with sound, give people a visible control to pause or stop it.',
    'Same id used twice' => 'Same id used twice',
    'Give every id on the page a value of its own. Repeated components such as cards and accordions are the usual cause: build the id from something unique, like the entry ID or the loop index.' => 'Give every id on the page a value of its own. Repeated components such as cards and accordions are the usual cause: build the id from something unique, like the entry ID or the loop index.',
    'No meta description' => 'No meta description',
    'Add a <meta name="description"> tag to the page\'s <head> with a sentence or two summing up the page. It is not a WCAG requirement, but search results and link previews show it.' => 'Add a <meta name="description"> tag to the page\'s <head> with a sentence or two summing up the page. It is not a WCAG requirement, but search results and link previews show it.',
    'Tab has no name' => 'Tab has no name',
    'Summary has no name' => 'Summary has no name',
    'Hidden content can take focus' => 'Hidden content can take focus',
    'Content inside aria-hidden="true" is hidden from screen readers, so nothing in it should take keyboard focus. Remove aria-hidden from the element, or move the links, buttons and form fields out of it.' => 'Content inside aria-hidden="true" is hidden from screen readers, so nothing in it should take keyboard focus. Remove aria-hidden from the element, or move the links, buttons and form fields out of it.',
    'List item outside a list' => 'List item outside a list',
    'Put every <li> directly inside a <ul> or <ol>. The usual cause is a template loop that outputs list items without the list around them, or a <div> sitting between the list and its items.' => 'Put every <li> directly inside a <ul> or <ol>. The usual cause is a template loop that outputs list items without the list around them, or a <div> sitting between the list and its items.',
    'Personal details field has no autocomplete' => 'Personal details field has no autocomplete',
    'Add an autocomplete attribute saying what the field collects, such as autocomplete="name", "email" or "tel", so browsers can fill it in. Where it fits, changing the field type to email or tel does the job too.' => 'Add an autocomplete attribute saying what the field collects, such as autocomplete="name", "email" or "tel", so browsers can fill it in. Where it fits, changing the field type to email or tel does the job too.',
    'Markup renders inside a code sample' => 'Markup renders inside a code sample',
    'Escape the angle brackets in the sample: write &lt; and &gt; in place of < and >. Wrapping markup in <code> or <pre> does not escape it, so the browser renders the tag instead of showing it.' => 'Escape the angle brackets in the sample: write &lt; and &gt; in place of < and >. Wrapping markup in <code> or <pre> does not escape it, so the browser renders the tag instead of showing it.',
    'Block element inside a paragraph' => 'Block element inside a paragraph',
    'Change the wrapping <p> to a <div>, or stop the content inside bringing its own paragraphs. This usually happens when a template wraps a rich text field, which outputs its own <p> tags, in another <p>.' => 'Change the wrapping <p> to a <div>, or stop the content inside bringing its own paragraphs. This usually happens when a template wraps a rich text field, which outputs its own <p> tags, in another <p>.',
    'Text contrast too low' => 'Text contrast too low',
    'Darken the text or lighten the background, or the other way round, until the contrast ratio is at least 4.5:1, or 3:1 for large text. Each finding gives the colours and ratio measured. Change the colour where your stylesheet defines it, so every use is fixed at once.' => 'Darken the text or lighten the background, or the other way round, until the contrast ratio is at least 4.5:1, or 3:1 for large text. Each finding gives the colours and ratio measured. Change the colour where your stylesheet defines it, so every use is fixed at once.',
    'Text contrast below the AAA level' => 'Text contrast below the AAA level',
    'Level AAA asks for a contrast ratio of at least 7:1, or 4.5:1 for large text. Darken the text or lighten the background until each finding reaches it.' => 'Level AAA asks for a contrast ratio of at least 7:1, or 4.5:1 for large text. Darken the text or lighten the background until each finding reaches it.',
    'Text contrast too low on hover' => 'Text contrast too low on hover',
    'The colours your stylesheet sets on hover fall below the contrast the text needs. Change the hover colour or background until the ratio reaches 4.5:1, or 3:1 for large text.' => 'The colours your stylesheet sets on hover fall below the contrast the text needs. Change the hover colour or background until the ratio reaches 4.5:1, or 3:1 for large text.',
    'Text contrast too low on focus' => 'Text contrast too low on focus',
    'The colours your stylesheet sets on keyboard focus fall below the contrast the text needs. Change the focus colour or background until the ratio reaches 4.5:1, or 3:1 for large text.' => 'The colours your stylesheet sets on keyboard focus fall below the contrast the text needs. Change the focus colour or background until the ratio reaches 4.5:1, or 3:1 for large text.',
    'Selected text contrast too low' => 'Selected text contrast too low',
    'The colours your stylesheet sets for selected text (::selection) fall below the contrast the text needs. Change them until the ratio reaches 4.5:1, or 3:1 for large text.' => 'The colours your stylesheet sets for selected text (::selection) fall below the contrast the text needs. Change them until the ratio reaches 4.5:1, or 3:1 for large text.',
